---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import Status from '../components/Status.astro';
import RainfallChart from '../components/RainfallChart.astro';
import { release, url } from '../lib/publication';
const find = (id: string) => release.claims.find(c => c.id === id);
const national = find('C-IMD-RAINFALL-DEP-india-20260923');
const east = find('C-IMD-RAINFALL-DEP-imd-east-northeast-20260923');
const south = find('C-IMD-RAINFALL-DEP-imd-south-peninsular-20260923');
const central = find('C-IMD-RAINFALL-DEP-imd-central-20260923');
const connection = find('C-JJM-CONNECTIONS-20260303');
const quality = find('C-JJM-FUNCTIONALITY-2024');
const funds = find('C-JJM-FUNDS-20260331');
const karnataka = find('C-KA-DROUGHT-ORDER-20260922');
const storageIndia = find('C-CWC-INDIA-STORAGE-20260910');
const storageSouth = find('C-CWC-SOUTH-STORAGE-20260910');
const source = (id: string) => url(`/sources/${find(id)?.evidenceIds[0] || ''}/`);
---
<Site title="The water question, across India" description="A dated, source-linked account of India's 2026 rainfall, water access and the evidence still needed to understand supply.">
  <section class="hero story-lead"><div class="shell hero-grid">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">India Water Watch · national briefing · evidence through 23 September 2026</p><h1>When the rain falls short, what happens to the water?</h1><p class="lede">India's latest reviewed monsoon snapshot shows a rainfall shortfall. The harder question—what that means for stored water, farms and taps—has no single national answer yet.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="button" href={url('/explore/')}>Explore the rainfall evidence <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button button-light" href={url('/states/')}>Find your state or UT</a></div></div>
    <aside class="hero-aside story-fact"><p class="eyebrow">The dated finding · IMD reported</p>{national ? <><strong class="story-fact-number">−14.9%</strong><p>All-India rainfall departure for 1 June–23 September 2026: 713.3 mm received against 837.7 mm normal for those dates, using IMD's 1971–2020 reference.</p><p class="story-fact-source"><a href={source(national.id)}>Inspect the IMD source and calculation ↗</a></p></> : <p>No national rainfall figure is approved in this build. <a href={url('/data-status/')}>Check coverage ↗</a></p>}<p class="small muted">This is rainfall, not a drought declaration or a measure of household supply. Provider graphics may be revised.</p></aside>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><Status /><nav class="story-index" aria-label="Story chapters"><p class="eyebrow">Follow the story</p><a href="#rainfall">01 · What the rain says</a><a href="#translation">02 · The missing links</a><a href="#people">03 · Water at home</a><a href="#response">04 · Public response</a><a href="#next">05 · What changes next</a></nav></div></section>
  <section class="section story-chapter" id="rainfall"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / The observed signal</p><h2>One country. Different departures.</h2></div><p>The all-India figure compresses substantial regional variation. These broad IMD regions are neither states nor service areas.</p></div>
    {national && east && south && central ? <p class="reading">Through 23 September, IMD reported departures of <strong>−26.5% in East & Northeast India</strong>, <strong>−25.7% in South Peninsular India</strong> and <strong>−5.3% in Central India</strong>. The regional graphic gives these percentages but not each region's cumulative normal total, so we attribute them to IMD rather than claiming to have independently reproduced every regional calculation. <a href={source(east.id)}>Regional graphic and limits ↗</a></p> : <p class="reading">Regional findings await approved evidence. <a href={url('/data-status/')}>See coverage ↗</a></p>}
    <RainfallChart />
    <div class="story-contrast grid-2"><div><p class="eyebrow">What this establishes</p><h3>Less rain than that date's normal</h3><p>The national millimetres and normal are printed in IMD's dated graphic. Their ratio reproduces the displayed rounded national percentage. <a href={national ? source(national.id) : url('/sources/')}>See the source ↗</a></p></div><div><p class="eyebrow">What it cannot establish</p><h3>Who has water at the tap</h3><p>Rain may enter different catchments, reservoirs and aquifers. Delivery and quality depend on systems this rainfall graphic does not observe. <a href={url('/understand/rain-to-tap/')}>Follow the chain ↗</a></p></div></div>
    {storageIndia && storageSouth && <div class="story-rail"><p class="eyebrow">A second system · CWC bulletin · 10 September 2026</p><h2>Rainfall and storage tell different parts of the story.</h2><div class="grid-2"><div><h3>178 monitored reservoirs nationwide</h3><p>CWC reported <strong>130.554 billion cubic metres</strong> of live storage, or <strong>70.66%</strong> of that monitored group's combined live capacity. This is a capacity fill measure for a named cohort, not a rainfall departure or all water available in India. <a href={source(storageIndia.id)}>CWC bulletin and denominator ↗</a></p></div><div><h3>50 in CWC's southern region</h3><p>CWC reported <strong>30.467 BCM</strong>, or <strong>54.52%</strong> of their combined live capacity; it was below that group's corresponding-week ten-year normal of 40.827 BCM. CWC's southern reservoir group and IMD's South Peninsular rainfall region cover different geographies, on different dates. <a href={source(storageSouth.id)}>Southern cohort and limits ↗</a></p></div></div><p class="small muted">The 10 September bulletin cannot show how storage changed by IMD's 23 September rainfall cutoff. Neither measure establishes delivery or quality at a household.</p></div>}
  </div></section>
  <section class="feature" id="translation"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / From weather to supply</p><h2>The missing links matter.</h2><p>To understand a specific water system, follow catchment rainfall into usable storage or groundwater, then through treatment and delivery. The approved CWC reservoir snapshot is dated 10 September, earlier than the 23 September rain cutoff; groundwater and local service still need separate evidence.</p><a href={url('/data-status/')}>See exactly what remains unmeasured ↗</a></div><div class="feature-graphic"><svg class="water-path" viewBox="0 0 430 230" role="img" aria-labelledby="diagram-title"><title id="diagram-title">Illustrative path from rain to household service; each link needs separate evidence</title><path d="M50 120 H380" stroke-dasharray="5 7"/><circle cx="55" cy="120" r="29"/><circle cx="160" cy="120" r="29"/><circle cx="270" cy="120" r="29"/><circle cx="375" cy="120" r="29"/><text x="23" y="185">Rain</text><text x="128" y="185">Catchment</text><text x="235" y="185">Storage</text><text x="355" y="185">Tap</text></svg></div></section>
  <section class="section story-chapter" id="people"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 / Water and people</p><h2>A connection is a beginning, not the end of the story.</h2></div><p>Different sources tell us about access at different dates. Their denominators cannot be joined into a single 2026 service rate.</p></div><div class="grid-2"><article class="editorial-card story-step"><p class="eyebrow">Reported · 3 March 2026</p><h3>About 15.82 crore rural households with tap connections</h3><p>States and UTs reported this out of about 19.36 crore rural households in a ministry parliamentary reply. It counts connections; it does not test daily reliability or safety. {connection && <a href={source(connection.id)}>Parliamentary reply ↗</a>}</p></article><article class="editorial-card story-step"><p class="eyebrow">Surveyed · July–October 2024</p><h3>Functionality needs separate checks</h3><p>In villages already recorded as covered, a sampled assessment found 86.5% of surveyed households with taps had received water in the preceding seven days. Its tested microbiological samples and quantity estimates have different denominators and methods. {quality && <a href={source(quality.id)}>Survey and caveats ↗</a>}</p></article></div><p class="note">Neither source measures what happened to a household after the September 2026 rainfall shortfall. <a href={url('/water-and-people/')}>Read the access story and its older survey context ↗</a></p></div></section>
  <section class="section story-chapter" id="response"><div class="shell grid-2"><div><p class="eyebrow">04 / The public record</p><h2>A documented declaration. Unanswered outcomes.</h2>{karnataka && <p>In a <a href={source(karnataka.id)}>22 September gazetted order</a>, Karnataka declared 53 additional taluks across 17 districts drought-affected for the 2026 kharif season. It authorizes relief and directs a crop-loss survey; the order does not show that aid was delivered or losses measured.</p>}<p>A separate <a href={funds ? source(funds.id) : url('/sources/')}>March 2026 ministry release</a> documented Jal Jeevan Mission 2.0 approval, guidelines and a reported fund release. That programme record is not proof of a September local intervention or improved household service.</p><a class="button" href={url('/response/')}>Read the action-stage tracker ↗</a></div><div class="empty-panel"><p class="eyebrow">Evidence test</p><ol class="timeline"><li>Declaration and legal authority</li><li>Sanction and funds released</li><li>Work or relief delivered in a named place</li><li>Outcome measured there</li></ol><p class="small">A declaration is a documented action. Relief delivery and crop or service outcomes still need separate records.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section story-chapter" id="next"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">05 / What comes next</p><h2>Watch the recovery, not just the deficit.</h2></div><p>Any outlook must be tied to its issue date and validity. A forecast is not an observed outcome.</p></div><div class="grid-3"><article class="editorial-card story-link-card"><p class="eyebrow">Outlook</p><h3><a class="title-link" href={url('/outlook/')}>Two possible paths</a></h3><p>What would strengthen concern in a particular supply system, and which observations would weaken it?</p></article><article class="editorial-card story-link-card"><p class="eyebrow">History</p><h3><a class="title-link" href={url('/history/')}>Has this happened before?</a></h3><p>Why a partial 2026 season cannot honestly be ranked against complete earlier monsoons.</p></article><article class="editorial-card story-link-card"><p class="eyebrow">Local view</p><h3><a class="title-link" href={url('/states/')}>Find your place</a></h3><p>See what a state page can show—and where district or service-area evidence is still absent.</p></article></div><div class="story-rail"><p class="eyebrow">For readers and reporters</p><p>Every published number has a dated source record. Download the reviewed observations, inspect the methods, or use the journalist desk to pursue unanswered local questions.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="button button-light" href={url('/sources/')}>Sources</a><a class="button button-light" href={url('/journalists/')}>Journalist desk</a><a class="button button-light" href={url('/updates/')}>Dated updates</a></div></div></div></section>
</Site>
